 Diwali stock picks 2026: Angel One's 8 ‘Shagun Ke Shares’ with up to 32% upside (AI-generated image) 
 Angel One recommends 8 festive picks with up to 32% upside.
 Nifty earnings projected to rebound by 15% in FY27.
 Diwali Muhurat trading is scheduled for November 8, 2026.
 Did our AI summary help? 
 Market Mastery
Indian equity markets have gone through a structural shift over the past few years, with domestic institutional investors (DIIs) and retail investors increasingly cushioning the impact of foreign fund outflows. As Indian markets head into Diwali 2026, domestic brokerage firm Angel One said Nifty earnings are expected to rebound by around 15 percent in FY27, supported by capital expenditure, investment activity and a recovery in consumption.
Against this backdrop, the brokerage sees opportunities across several sectors spanning, banks and NBFCs, auto, capital goods and defence, cement, power, consumer, healthcare, IT and telecom. It's eight festive-season picks – ‘Shagun Ke Shares’ as called by the brokerage - reflect this optimism, each positioned for fresh momentum into Samvat 2083.
 Diwali stock picks 2026: Eight stock recommendations by Angel One with up to 32% upside 
Angel One has highlighted opportunities across eight stocks, citing earnings growth potential, improving profitability, business expansion and relatively attractive valuations.
 1. ICICI Bank: Target Price Rs 1,800, upside 32% 
Angel One values ICICI Bank at Rs 1,800, based on 18.8x its estimated FY29 earnings per share (EPS) of Rs 95.7, assuming mid-teens earnings growth. ICICI Bank, India's second-largest private-sector bank, with a market capitalisation of about Rs 10 lakh crore and a pan-India retail, SME and corporate franchise, raised about US$18 billion of FCNR(B) deposits through the RBI swap facility in Q2 FY27. This supported deposit growth of 27.1% and loan growth of 30%. Excluding FCNR-related deposits and loans, the respective growth rates stood at 17% and 24.1%.
“This gives stable three-to-five-year funding, but it diluted NIM to 4.18% from 4.36% (about 4.28% excluding a Q1 tax refund) by adding term deposits and lower-yielding overseas assets. Management expects the full effect in Q3 FY27 and a recovery from Q4 as the funds are deployed and costlier deposits retired,” according to the brokerage.
 2. Northern Arc: Target Price Rs 330, upside 29% 
Angel One said it is optimistic on Northern Arc with a 'Buy' rating set a target price of Rs 330, based on approximately 6.1 times its estimated FY29 EPS of Rs 54. "We see scope for sustained earnings compounding as lending AUM grows approximately 20% a year to around Rs 28,600 crore by FY29E and direct-to-customer lending lifts NIM towards 10%. ROE should rise from 11% to ~16% as credit costs ease. The valuation remains reasonable relative to this profile," it added.
 3. Aarti Pharmalabs: Target Price Rs 1,160, upside 32% 
Angel One has initiated coverage on Aarti Pharmalabs, India’s largest manufacturer of xanthine derivatives (caffeine and allied products), with a 15–20 percent global market share, with a 'Buy' rating and gave a target price of rs 1,160, valuing the stock at 24 times its estimated FY29 EPS of Rs 48. The stock trades at approximately 17.1 times earnings, according to the brokerage.
"We see scope for earnings to recover as the company moves up the value chain from xanthine and APIs into CDMO. CDMO is guided to grow 40–50% in FY27 and standalone EBITDA margins to reach 22–25%. The valuation remains reasonable relative to ROE recovering from 8.5% to 15%," it added.
 4. Shanti Gold: Target Price Rs 410, upside 30% 
Angel One has recommended Shanti Gold with a 'Buy' rating and a target price of Rs 410, based on 10.5x its estimated FY29 EPS of Rs 39. "We see scope for sustained volume-led compounding as new capacity (Marol and Jaipur) and new retail customers support 50–60% FY27 revenue growth. The valuation remains reasonable relative to ROE of 38%, but upside is modest after the sharp re-rating since August," it added.
 5. Ratnaveer Precision: Target Price Rs 400, upside 16% 
Angel One has initiated coverage on Ratnaveer Precision with a 'Buy' rating and a target price of Rs 400, based on 30x its estimated FY29 EPS of Rs 13.4. “We see scope for earnings to compound as the core washer business grows and the Copper Clad Laminate project, with production from November 2026, adds a higher-margin electronics stream. Execution on the CCL ramp-up is the key swing factor,” it added.
